    "https://nshe.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Nevada-Reno---Main-Campus/Student-Worker---Fire-Extinguisher-Maintenance-Support---Facilities-Maintenance-Services_R0153400": {
      "title": "Student Worker – Fire Extinguisher Maintenance Support – Facilities Maintenance Services",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nPart time\n\nThe University of Nevada, Reno (UNR) appreciates your interest in employment at our growing institution. We want your application process to go smoothly and quickly. Final applications must be submitted prior to the close of the recruitment. If you need assistance or have questions regarding the application process, please contact our recruitment helpline at (775) 784-1495 or jobs@unr.edu . Job Description The University of Nevada, Reno is recruiting students interested in employment in the Facilities Maintenance Services Department within the Fire, Life, and Safety unit to support the fire extinguisher maintenance program. Responsibilities Assist the Fire Extinguisher Technician with maintenance and inspection activities Ride in the service vehicle with the technician while traveling to various campus locations Retrieve fire extinguishers from campus buildings and transport them to the service truck or designated maintenance area Return serviced extinguishers to their correct locations Read and interpret building floor plans to identify extinguisher locations Tag or mark extinguisher locations for easy identification and tracking Lift and carry fire extinguishers safely to and from the service vehicle Operate or ride in a golf cart when necessary to access locations throughout campus, including areas with busy pedestrian traffic Exercise caution and follow campus safety procedures when traveling through pedestrian areas Follow all safety procedures and instructions provided by the technician Provide general assistance as needed to support the campus fire extinguisher maintenance program; and Other duties as assigned. Physical Demands & Working Conditions Walking or standing to a significant degree; Pushing and/or pulling; Exerting 50 to 100 pounds of force occasionally, and/or 25 to 50 pounds of force frequently, and/or 10 to 20 pounds of force constantly to move objects. Required Qualifications Candidate must be enrolled at the University of Nevada, Reno; Candidate must be dependable, punctual, and detail-oriented This position is subject to pre-employment, post-accident and reasonable suspicion drug and alcohol test. The candidate selected for hire will be required to sign a form acknowledging this policy. A valid Class “C” driver’s license or higher operator’s license is required at the time of appointment and as a condition of continuing employment. The successful candidates must complete the Defensive Driving course shortly after hire. Driving carts on busy campus roads along with pedestrians is required for this position. Schedule Hours: Monday – Friday between the hours of 7:00 am to 3:30 pm During Semester: Up to 25 hours a week During Breaks: Up to 40 hours a week Compensation Grade Student Employee Level 2 $14/hr. Exempt No Full-Time Equivalent 0.0% Required Attachment(s) Please note, once you submit your application the only attachment/s viewable to you will be the attachment/s to the resume/CV section of the application. Any additional required attachment/s to the cover letter, references, additional documents sections of the application, will not be viewable to you after you submit your application. All uploaded attachment/s will be on the application for the committee to review. To request updates to attachments, prior to review of applications, please contact the candidate helpdesk at jobs@unr.edu . Attach the following attachment(s) to your application Resume/CV – (required) List a detailed description of the major duties that you performed as part of each job. You must demonstrate that you qualify for the position and your education and experience must be clearly documented. Cover Letter – (optional) This posting is open until filled Qualified individuals are encouraged to apply immediately. This search will close without notice when a sufficient number of applications are received or a hiring decision has been made. Posting 