    "https://nshe.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Nevada-Reno---Main-Campus/Grants---Projects-Analyst-2---College-of-Engineering_R0153249": {
      "title": "Grants & Projects Analyst 2 – College of Engineering",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe University of Nevada, Reno (UNR) appreciates your interest in employment at our growing institution. We want your application process to go smoothly and quickly. Final applications must be submitted prior to the close of the recruitment. If you need assistance or have questions regarding the application process, please contact our recruitment helpline at (775) 784-1495 or jobs@unr.edu . Job Description The University of Nevada, Reno is accepting applications for a Grants & Projects Analyst 2 to join the College of Engineering. This position plays a vital role in supporting faculty and staff throughout the grant proposal process. Responsibilities include managing complex grant functions, ensuring compliance with university and sponsor regulations, and maintaining detailed informational and financial records. The analyst oversees proposal intake and faculty communications and leads the submission of complete proposal packages through various electronic systems. Additional duties include reviewing funding opportunities, developing and checking proposal budgets, and assisting with sponsor-specific documentation. The analyst serves as the primary budget contact during planning meetings and works closely with Sponsored Projects and faculty to ensure smooth coordination. This role also supports training and outreach by providing guidance to principal investigators, staff, and students on sponsor requirements and grant procedures. The analyst helps streamline proposal development through improved communication strategies and collaborates with college communications staff to promote faculty research. They may also present research data and outcomes to internal and external audiences. This position provides backup support for post-award activities such as processing project extensions, budget modifications, and reviewing monthly reports. Other research-related duties may be assigned as needed. This position is full-time and provides layoff rights. Essential Qualifications Bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university in public or business administration, accounting, finance or related field and two (2) years of professional grants experience which includes at least two of the following areas: writing grant applications; determining grant/subgrant program eligibility; researching, writing and implementing grant program plans; managing fiscal aspects of grants/subgrants; providing technical assistance to grant/subgrant recipients; and/or monitoring and ensuring grant/subgrant recipient compliance; OR Graduation from high school or equivalent education and four (4) years of professional grants experience which includes at least two of the areas as described above; OR One (1) year of experience as a Grants & Projects Analyst I in Nevada State service; OR An equivalent combination of education and experience as described above. Preferred Qualifications Candidates with one or more of the following qualifications are encouraged to apply:  Knowledge of federal grant regulations (e.g., Uniform Guidance, NIH, NSF), post-award processes, and university research administration practices. Experience in pre- and post-award grant management, including budget development, financial reporting, and compliance monitoring. Proficiency with ERP systems (e.g., Workday, PeopleSoft, Banner), Microsoft Excel (pivot tables, vlookups), and data visualization tools like Power BI or Tableau. Strong analytical, communication, and organizational skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities and collaborate across teams. Schedule The typical work schedule is Monday through Friday from 8:00 am to 5:00 pm; this is subject to change based on organizational needs. Compensation Grade Grade 35 In classified service, salary is in Grade and Step. The Step is determined based on the Nevada Administrative Code. Salary placement above a Step 01 at initial appointment is determined based on the recruitment, the candidate’s qualifications, internal equity, and budgets. A request to accelerate salary must be approved by Human Resources and abide by the Nevada Administrative Code. To view the classified compensation schedules, please visit: Classified Compensation . Select Salary schedule, PP01. For more information, visit the Classified Salary Calculator The Perks of PERS Classified Employees are enrolled in The Public Employees’ Retirement System of Nevada (PERS) upon hire. The PERS retirement plan is beyond compare. Please visit the Benefit Estimator Retirement Calculator for more information. Perks of Working at UNR Health insurance options including dental and vision - Health Insurance Life insurance, generous annual and sick leave - Classified Benefits E. L. Wiegand Fitness Center offers annual or semester memberships and spouse/domestic partner membership options .  E.L. Wiegand Fitness Center Mountain EAP supports employees (and eligible dependents) through life's difficult moments. Mountain EAP is located in Reno and specializes in counseling and advising services for personal or interpersonal issues. Staff Employees’ Council (SEC) represents all Classified employees. SEC holds monthly meetings to provide a forum for employees to participate. SEC Classified Staff Grants-In-Aid Benefit For more information about the Classified Staff Grant-In-Aid Benefit, please visit: Classified Staff Grants-In-Aid Benefit Classified Employee Family Opportunity Program Additionally, we offer a Classified Employee Family Opportunity Program for spouses, domestic partners, and dependents of classified employees (working at least a 50% full-time equivalent). For more information, please visit: Classified Employee Family Opportunity Program Department Information Join the College of Engineering at the University of Nevada, Reno and become part of a team dedicated to innovation, research, and student success. Our classified staff play an essential role in supporting the college's mission through administrative, technical, and operational excellence. Nevada Engineering is committed to improving the lives of Nevadans through education, research, and economic development. The college fosters a supportive and inclusive workplace through initiatives that promote professional development, employee engagement, and collaboration across departments. Classified staff enjoy a comprehensive benefits package, including health insurance, participation in the Nevada Public Employees’ Retirement System (PERS), and Grants-in-Aid tuition benefits for courses within the Nevada System of Higher Education (NSHE). As one of the University's 13 colleges and schools, Nevada Engineering is home to nationally recognized research centers and laboratories that support cutting-edge research and industry partnerships. In FY25, the college secured approximately $30 million in research awards. Student success remains at the heart of everything we do. The college offers 12 degree programs, including new programs in aerospace engineering and industrial engineering, helping prepare the next generation of engineers to meet the needs of Nevada and beyond. For more information, please visit unr.edu/engineering . Contact Information Kristy McLean - kristymclean@unr.edu Exempt No Full-Time Equivalent 100.0% Required Attachment(s) Please note, once you submit your application the only attachment/s viewable to you will be the attachment/s to the resume/CV section of the application. Any additional required attachment/s to the cover letter, references, additional documents sections of the application, will not be viewable to you after you submit your application. All uploaded attachment/s will be on the application for the committee to review. To request updates to attachments, prior to the committee review of applications, please contact the candidate helpdesk at jobs@unr.edu . Attach the following attachment(s) to your application Resume/CV – (required) List a detailed description of the major duties that you performed as part of each job. You must demonstrate that you qualify for the position and your education and experience must be clearly documented. Cover Letter – (optional) Contact Information for Three Supervisory References – (required) Please make a note if you do not want your present employer contacted unless necessary to determine your qualifications for the position. Transcripts – (optional) If you have not graduated, please attach your transcripts to receive education credit for classes you have taken. Credit is given for classes relevant to the position. Veteran Interview Consideration – (optional) – To receive interview consideration for veterans and veterans with a service-connected disability, proof is required at the time of application. Please attach proof electronically to your application under the Veteran Document(s) section. (Examples of acceptable documents include DD-214, disability letter from Veteran's Administration, etc). This posting is open until filled Qualified individuals are encouraged to apply immediately. Lists of eligible candidates will be established and hiring may occur early in the recruiting process. Recruitment will close without notice when a sufficient number of applications are received, or a hiring decision has been made. Posting Close Date Note to Applicant A background check will be conducted on the candidate(s) selected for hire.    HR will attempt to verify academic credentials upon receipt of hiring documents. If the academic credentials cannot be verified, HR will notify the faculty member that an official transcript of their highest degree must be submitted within thirty days of the faculty member’s first day of employment.    References will be contacted at the appropriate phase of the recruitment process. Applicants hired on a federal contract may be subject to E-Verify.    As part of the hiring process, applicants for positions in the Nevada System of 