    "https://nshe.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Nevada-Reno---Main-Campus/Student-Worker---Parking-Enforcement-Officer--Parking-and-Transportation-Services_R0153035": {
      "title": "Student Worker - Parking Enforcement Officer, Parking and Transportation Services",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-10\nPosted: Posted 26 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe University of Nevada, Reno (UNR) appreciates your interest in employment at our growing institution. We want your application process to go smoothly and quickly. Final applications must be submitted prior to the close of the recruitment. If you need assistance or have questions regarding the application process, please contact our recruitment helpline at (775) 784-1495 or jobs@unr.edu . Job Description The Parking & Transportation Department is seeking students interested in employment in a Parking Enforcement position on campus. Responsibilities Enforce parking regulations and issue warnings and citations; Assist with general campus questions from students, staff, and visitors; Assist motorists with basic vehicle issues (battery jump, locked out of vehicle, etc.); Monitor bike racks and issue warnings when necessary; and Work large events including football games. Required Qualifications Candidate must be enrolled at the University of Nevada, Reno Candidate must have excellent customer service and communication skills A valid Class “C” driver’s license or higher operator’s license is required at the time of appointment and as a condition of continuing employment. The successful candidates must complete the Defensive Driving course shortly after hire. Driving carts on busy campus roads along with pedestrians is required for this position. Physical Demands & Working Conditions Walking or standing to a significant degree Pushing and/or pulling Exerting 25 to 50 pounds of force occasionally, and/or 20 to 25 pounds of force frequently, and/or 10 to 20 pounds of force constantly to move objects Exposure to hot and cold temperatures when working outside Schedule Hours: Monday – Thursday 4:00 pm to 8:00 pm During Semester: Up to 25 hours a week During Breaks: Up to 40 hours a week *This is subject to change based on organizational needs. Compensation Grade Student Level 1 $13.00/hr. 